# =============================================================================
# Sencha — build artifacts & local noise
# =============================================================================
# Always build out-of-source:
#   cmake -S . -B build
#   cmake --build build
#
# To clean ignored junk (WARNING: deletes ALL ignored files, not just build/):
#   git clean -ndX        # dry run — review first
#   git clean -fdX        # actually delete
# Or just:
#   rm -rf build build-release build-*
# =============================================================================

# Out-of-source build / output / install trees. Generated CMake/Ninja/Make
# files all live inside these, so they need no rules of their own as long as
# builds stay out-of-source.
#
# Anchored to the root, and each nested build tree named explicitly. These
# patterns used to match at any depth, which reads as the safer choice and is
# not: "build" is an ordinary word for a source directory, and an unanchored
# rule swallows one silently. engine/include/world/build/ went untracked that
# way, and the first sign of it was a CI checkout failing to compile against a
# header that exists on every machine that ever wrote it. A stray build tree
# committed from a subdirectory is a loud diff; source that never reaches the
# repository is not.
/build*/
/out*/
/install*/
template/build/
_deps/

# In-source configure safety net (the root CMakeLists forbids in-source builds,
# but ignore the stragglers in case someone runs configure in the wrong place).
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
Testing/

# CodeQL scratch dirs.
_codeql_build_dir/
_codeql_detected_source_root

# clangd / compile database (per-build; commit a top-level one by hand if wanted).
compile_commands.json
.cache/
.clangd/

# Coverage / profiling.
*.gcda
*.gcno
*.gcov
*.profdata
*.profraw

# IDE / editor.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.user.*
CMakeSettings.json

# OS cruft.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# AI / agent tool directories.
.codex
.claude/
.agents/
.copilot/

# Logs & temporaries.
*.log
*.tmp
*.swp
*~

# Dear ImGui window-layout dump written when running the editor
imgui.ini

# Core dumps. Valgrind writes one per intentional-abort test (the death tests
# that assert in debug), so a memcheck run over the suite leaves several behind.
vgcore.*
core.*

# Captured with a project open, per editor. data_editor has none yet.
data_editor.imgui.ini
